+      body: "A workflow takes form submissions, enrols the learner in the LMS, and sends a welcome email. One afternoon the LMS API times out midway through a batch. The retry logic re-runs the whole workflow from the trigger, so learners who had already been enrolled are enrolled again and emailed again. Nothing crashed and no error appeared. The fix has two parts: check whether the enrolment already exists before creating it, and retry the failed step rather than the whole run. The general rule underneath is that a retry is only safe when the operation is safe to repeat.",
